
{% embed '_partials/conditional_parent_or_file_form_wrapper.html.twig' with {
    'form': estCAForm,
    'form_name': 'estCAForm',
    'job_type_config': 'ClusterAnalysis-form'
} %}

    {% block description %}
        <p style="color: red">
        <b>
        An input SSN from the EFI-EST FASTA option should be generated using "Read
        FASTA headers" from FASTA files with UniProt IDs in the headers.  Otherwise,
        sets of IDs and sequences, MSAs, WebLogos, HMMs, consensus residues, and length
        histograms will not be generated.
        </b>
        </p>

        <p>
        <b>
        Like the Color SSN utility, clusters in the submitted SSN are identified, 
        numbered and colored.
        </b>
        </p>

        <p>
        The SSN clusters are numbered and colored using two conventions:
        <b>Sequence Count Cluster Numbers</b>
        are assigned in order of decreasing number of UniProt IDs in 
        the cluster; <b>Node Count Cluster Numbers</b> are assigned in order of decreasing 
        number of nodes in the cluster. 
        </p>

        <p>
        <b>
        Multiple sequence alignments (MSAs), WebLogos, hidden Markov models (HMMs), 
        length histograms, and consensus residues are computed for each cluster. 
        </b>
        </p>

        <p>
        Options are available in the tabs below to select the desired analyses:
        </p>

        <p>
        The <b>WebLogos</b> tab provides the WebLogo and MSA for the node IDs in each cluster 
        containing greater than the "<b>Minimum Node Count</b>" specified in the
        <b>Sequence Filter</b> tab.
        The percent identity matrix for the MSA is also provided on this tab.
        </p>

        <p>
        The <b>Consensus Residues</b> tab provides a tab-delimited text file with the number 
        of the conserved residues and their MSA positions for each specified residue in 
        each cluster containing greater than the "<b>Minimum Node Count</b>".  Note the 
        default residue is "C" and the percent identity levels that are displayed are 
        from 90 to 10% in intervals of 10%; a residue is counted as "conserved" if it 
        occurs with &ge;80% identity.
        </p>

        <p>
        The <b>HMMs</b> tab provides the HMM for each cluster containing greater than the 
        specified "<b>Minimum Node Count</b>". 
        </p>

        <p>
        The <b>Length Histograms</b> tab provides length histograms for each cluster 
        containing greater than the specified "<b>Minimum Node Count</b>". 
        </p>
    {% endblock %}

    {% block additional_fields %}
        <div data-controller="accordion" data-accordion-initially-open-value="true">
            <h3>Sequence Filter</h3>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <div>
                    <p>
                     The MSA is generated with MUSCLE using the node IDs. Clusters
                     containing less than the Minimum Node Count will be excluded
                     from the analyses. Since MUSCLE can fail with a "large" number
                     sequences (variable; anywhere from >750 to 1500), the Maximum
                     Node Count parameter can be used to limit the number of
                     sequences that MUSCLE uses.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="input-name">Minimum Node Count:</span>
                    <span class="input-field">
                        {{ form_widget(estCAForm.minNumSequences) }}
                    </span>
                    <label for="{{ estCAForm.minNumSequences.vars.id }}">Minimum number of nodes in order to include a cluster in the computations [default: {{ app_constants.DEFAULT_MIN_NUM_SEQUENCES }}].</label>
                </div>
                <div class="submission-error">{{ form_errors(estCAForm.minNumSequences) }}</div>
                <div>
                    <span class="input-name">Maximum Node Count:</span>
                    <span class="input-field">
                        {{ form_widget(estCAForm.maxNumSequences) }}
                    </span>
                    <label for="{{ estCAForm.maxNumSequences.vars.id }}">Maximum number of nodes to include in the MSA [default: no maximum].</label>
                </div>
                <div class="submission-error">{{ form_errors(estCAForm.maxNumSequences) }}</div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div data-controller="accordion">
            <h3>WebLogos</h3>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <div>
                    <p>A MSA for the (length-filtered) node IDs is generated using MUSCLE; the WebLogo
                    is generated with the <a href="http://weblogo.threeplusone.com">http://weblogo.threeplusone.com</a> code.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    {{ form_row(estCAForm.makeWeblogo) }}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div data-controller="accordion">
            <h3>Consensus Residues</h3>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <div>
                    <p>The positions and selected percent identities of the selected residues in the MSA are determined.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <div>
                        {{ form_row(estCAForm.computeConsensusResidues) }}
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        {{ form_row(estCAForm.consensusResidues) }}
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <span class="input-name">Percent Identity Thresholds:</span>
                    {{ form_row(estCAForm.pidThresholds) }}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div data-controller="accordion">
            <h3>HMMs</h3>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <div>
                    <p>The MSA for the (length-filtered) node IDs is used to generate the HMM with
                    <i>hmmbuild</i> from <a href="http://hmmer.org">HMMER3 (http://hmmer.org)</a>.</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    {{ form_row(estCAForm.makeHmms) }}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div data-controller="accordion">
            <h3>Length Histograms</h3>
            <div class="accordion-content">
                <div>
                    <p>Length histograms for the node IDs (where applicable, UniProt, UniRef90, and UniRef50 IDs).</p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    {{ form_row(estCAForm.makeLengthHistograms) }}
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    {% endblock %}

{% endembed %}

